+### Phase 1: Tests First (TDD)
+
+- [ ] T001 [P] Write the failing authenticated-callback integration test for `POST /callbacks/reminder`.
+
+**Implements**: FR-001, FR-004
+
+**Scenario**: Send one provider-shaped callback with a valid signature and one with a missing, malformed, or mismatched signature. The valid callback may proceed to the service boundary; every invalid callback is rejected before a `delivery_events` row is persisted.
+
+**Pattern**: Use the repository’s real HTTP test client and its provider-secret test configuration. Construct the signature over the exact raw body sent to the route; do not test a helper in isolation as a substitute for the HTTP boundary.
+
+**Security**: Assert that failure responses do not expose the expected signature or secret and that no event is written for the invalid request.
+
+**File**: `tests/integration/reminders/delivery-callback-auth.test.ts`
+
+- [ ] T002 [P] Write the failing request-role integration test for workspace-scoped `GET /actions/{id}/delivery`.
+
+**Implements**: FR-005
+
+**Scenario**: Seed an action and its delivery event in workspace A. Read it as a workspace-A request principal and assert the persisted status is returned. Repeat as a workspace-B request principal and assert the API’s ordinary denial/not-found response with no delivery payload.
+
+**Pattern**: Use the request-role fixture or connection, never an admin/service-role client. The test must make the actual GET request and prove the authorization boundary rather than querying the table directly.
+
+**File**: `tests/integration/reminders/delivery-status-authorization.test.ts`
